--- body ---
## Evidence gap

The legacy `events.csv` row `zaf-murp-afdb-approved-2026` records a USD 400
million AfDB approval for Mpumalanga municipal utility reform, dated
2026-07-16. Its `source_id` is `zaf-murp-afdb-2026`, but the legacy row has
no `document_sha256` and only the broad locator “official announcement.”
Ticket [[0926]] subsequently collected the publisher HTML: retrieval
`zaf-murp-afdb-2026:2` at `data/jetp/retrievals.csv:321` is HTTP 200 via
`browser-session`, with SHA-256
`a9385e879af5f88511324674b8b12345cea23bc3dd0fbc8eae3b02a11e57cf33`.
The corresponding `manifest.csv:321` entry names
`objects/a9/a9385e879af5f88511324674b8b12345cea23bc3dd0fbc8eae3b02a11e57cf33.html`.
Collection closed the snapshot gap; it did not supply a cited line or a
reviewed agreement identity. The 0876 pending register therefore reports
`missing_precise_cited_line`, and the event must not become an observation
from the headline alone.

## Work

- Materialize the archived HTML with `make jetp-data`; inspect its rendered
  article body and identify the exact approval statement, date, amount,
  instrument, borrower/beneficiary, and any distinction between loan approval,
  signature, and disbursement.
- Add a ledger line with the archived SHA and a precise paragraph or heading
  locator. Adjudicate the subject as a distinct agreement, an existing
  agreement, or a source-row-only referent, documenting the identity basis.
- Add the event-specific decision for 0876 and regenerate its pending and
  reconciliation outputs. Preserve the legacy source view bytes and leave
  unsupported financial stages pending.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The archived publisher statement, exact locator, snapshot hash, and
  financial stage are recorded in a cited ledger line.
- [ ] The event has one reviewed subject decision with a line-referent, or
  an explicit documented reason to keep it pending.
- [ ] The 0876 register and all 451 legacy timing rows reconcile after
  rebuild; no approval is promoted to signature or disbursement.
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, focused source/reconciliation tests,
  `make check-fast`, and `make lint` run; any full-gate obstacle is recorded
  by test or preflight ID.
